WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.934
-Welcome back to the show
in person.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.267
-Thank you! I know!

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.701
-I mean...
-We're back.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.467
-You're back in New York City.
-Here we are.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.033
-This is your hometown.
-This is it.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:10.501
-How's it feel?
-Feels great.

00:00:10.501 --> 00:00:12.434
-It does, right?
-It feels amazing.

00:00:12.434 --> 00:00:14.567
-I wanted to ask you because
tonight's a big show for us.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.000
We have -- obviously, you're on.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.601
But I mean, we have, the Olympic
opening ceremonies was tonight

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:22.934
and I heard that you were almost
in an Olympic commercial once.

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:24.100
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.634
-Is that true?
-Yes.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.634
Well, I was in
an Olympic commercial.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.634
-You were?
-I don't think it aired.

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:31.968
Because I might -- I --

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.601
[ Laughs ]
Okay, so here's the story.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.601
The story is I went in
to audition

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.067
and you know, when you first
start auditioning,

00:00:39.067 --> 00:00:42.100
I went in as a dancer
and kind of like whatever.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.901
And they were like,
"Okay, can you dance?"

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.267
I danced and then I talked
and I read the copy

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:48.767
and I did the things,
and then they were like,

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:51.000
"By the way" -- I'm walking out
and I'm like, I nailed this.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.367
I killed this.
-I got this.

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.467
-I got this.
I was great today.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.167
Today was my day.
-Yes, exactly.

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.868
-I'm walking out and I'm like,
"Okay, bye, thank you.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:01.033
Thank you so much. Thank you."
And I walk out

00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.267
and the guy says to me,
right before I leave, he goes,

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:05.767
"Hey, by the way,
can you do trampoline?"

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.868
And I go, "Yeah."

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.367
And I walk out,
thinking nothing of it.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:11.567
-Sure. Yeah.

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.000
-Can I do a trampoline?
Are you kidding me?

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.434
-I get there and I do
all the things, I dance, I sing,

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.367
and then they bring out this
trampoline and they're like,

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.601
"Okay!"
-"Let's see what you got."

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:22.000
-"Do it!"

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.467
And I was like...okay.

00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:27.334
They're like, "You know, you do
the flips and the things."

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:30.801
And I was like, "Sure,
I'll do the trampoline."

00:01:30.801 --> 00:01:32.634
I get up there and I'm like...

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.601
That was it.
That's all I had.

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:40.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:42.300
-Cut to c--
Is that all she does?

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.534
Did she do the trampoline?
-I did this!

00:01:43.534 --> 00:01:45.701
I did this, I jumped,
and I did some of this.

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.434
-You posed.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:48.968
-It was awful.
-That's not doing trampoline.

00:01:48.968 --> 00:01:51.367
-And they were like, "You said
you could do trampoline."

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.601
And I said, "No, I..."
-I'm sorry.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.534
-I did, but I didn't know
what you meant.

00:01:56.534 --> 00:01:58.100
-How's the fam?

00:01:58.100 --> 00:01:59.634
-Everybody's good.
-Two teenagers.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:01.300
-I know.
-Wow, is that wild.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:04.400
-I know, does anybody else
have teenagers right now?

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Laughs ]

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.567
-It's interesting, right?
-It is. It is.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:10.367
You know, they go from like
being these babies,

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:12.667
and then when they turn
like 11 1/2, 12,

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:15.501
they become like adult people
in a little body.

00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:17.100
-I know, I know.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.934
I'm like -- every second,
I love hanging out with my kids

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.601
because I just don't want you
to grow up, but I do.

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:24.133
-What they do is
that they need to, like,

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.901
distance themselves a little.
You know, it's my life.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.767
I have my own identity.

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.968
I am who I am, this is what
I feel about the world.

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:33.234
This is what I think.
And, you know, it's like,

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:34.567
Oh, my God, and I'm like,

00:02:34.567 --> 00:02:36.234
"Baby, you want to sit
on my lap?"

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.400
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.567
-No, I don't now.
I'm a teenager. Not at all.

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:41.634
-Mom, stop. Stop touching me.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.167
-I'll tell you
who is here tonight --

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.334
your mom is here.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.334
-Who also likes me
to still sit on her lap.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.000
-Lupe is here tonight.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:49.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.000
-Hi, Mom.
-Hi, beautiful.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.167
Oh, my god, she is
the prettiest, the coolest.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.000
Is that --

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.133
Is that where you get
your drive? Is that --

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:01.267
-From my mom?
-Yeah.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:02.601
-Where do you think?
-I think I get my --

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.868
like, my personality
from my mom, a little bit.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:09.701
And you know, both my mom
and dad worked really hard.

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.934
-Yeah.
-So I definitely --

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.634
-I don't know anyone
that works as hard as you.

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:14.133
-I know. I don't know
what's wrong with me.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.267
I'm not well.
-No, you are unbelievable.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:17.801
But I've known you
since "Saturday Night Live,"

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.534
but I've seen in every --
-I know.

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:20.934
-Every aspect,
and you're just there

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.767
and you're just mentally
in the game and you're like,

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:25.200
"Yeah, cool. What's up?
We'll do that," blah blah.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.734
-What's next? Let's do it!
-"We'll do this. What's next?"

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:28.067
-I go...
-This is fun!

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.234
-But like, "Marry Me."

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.734
You go, "Great,
I'm in this movie."

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.400
That's enough for me.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.701
-I mean, I grew up in the Bronx.

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:35.400
My mom'll tell you,
we grew up in the Bronx.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.067
We really didn't have a lot.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:39.033
You know,
this is a dream come true.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.200
Everything I do,
every single day,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.133
I feel so incredibly blessed.

00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:45.334
I feel so lucky to be doing
what I'm doing.

00:03:45.334 --> 00:03:47.300
I always wanted to sing.
I always wanted to dance.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.334
My mother loved musicals,
you know,

00:03:49.334 --> 00:03:52.100
she showed me them from
when I was very, very little,

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.400
and I just had all these dreams
of like doing that.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:57.734
And so now I'm doing it.
So why not do it all the time?

00:03:57.734 --> 00:03:59.934
I'll do it all the time.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.834
You got it. Everybody knows.
-Yeah, yeah. But I mean...

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.634
-You guys -- The Roots want
to play all the time.

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:07.234
-Yeah.
-All they want to do is play.

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:08.901
Every chance you get
to pick up a guitar,

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.601
whether you're playing or not,
whether you're at work,

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.367
you're doing what you love.
-You just want to do, like...

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:14.601
Just play.
-Yeah. You know that.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:17.267
-I know, but you also did
the soundtrack to this.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.467
-I did.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.801
-You and Maluma are all over --
this is all you.

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:22.267
And this is out now.

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:23.801
The movie comes out next week.
-Yes! Look at it!

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.300
Yay!
-Ah, there you go!

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.634
-It never gets old for me.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:31.868
Yes, this was actually
the first time

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:34.033
since I did the movie "Selena"
where I actually got to --

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.400
I didn't sing
in the movie "Selena."

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.067
That was Selena's voice.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.434
-So this is the first time
I got to, like, sing,

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.634
make an album for a film.

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.767
It is like joining
my two worlds together.

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.100
I also got to play a character

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.667
who was, you know,
a lot like myself.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.167
You know,
she's in the spotlight,

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:54.467
personal life, public life,
trying to make it all work.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:56.901
You know,
failing miserably at times.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:58.701
You know what I mean?
Doing all the things.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:00.200
But it's a really,

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:03.501
really great kind of look
behind the behind the scenes.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:04.834
-Yeah, I remember the last time

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.934
you were here with Maluma.
-Yes.

00:05:07.934 --> 00:05:09.601
-You actually had a scene
in the movie

00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:10.968
where you're supposed
to be at a concert.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.801
You guys are doing your famous
duet in character.

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:13.968
-Yeah.

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.601
-And instead of re-creating
a fake concert

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:19.100
on a movie set somewhere,
you crashed Maluma's --

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:22.100
-Oh, I did. We did.
-...Maluma's concert.

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:25.334
-Yes, he was having like two
nights at Madison Square Garden.

00:05:25.334 --> 00:05:27.601
And of course,
the producer in me is like,

00:05:27.601 --> 00:05:29.367
"We can take advantage of that."
-[ Laughing ] Yeah, yeah.

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:30.934
It's like, yeah.
Alright, he's already got --

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:33.734
-We have a scene, a big scene
in an arena.

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:35.234
Why don't we do it
at your concert?

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:38.167
And he was like, "Okay..."
-Yeah.

00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.634
-How'd that feel?
People must have went bonkers --

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:41.968
-It was amazing.
-...when you walked out.

00:05:41.968 --> 00:05:43.634
-It was amazing, yeah.
I came up out of the floor

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:45.467
dressed like the character
in the movie,

00:05:45.467 --> 00:05:46.901
and this scene is in the movie.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:50.067
And they just didn't expect me
to come out at his concert.

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.100
I've never been out
at one of his concerts.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.934
And the crowd went wild,

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.734
and we got it all on film
and we sang together.

00:05:56.734 --> 00:05:58.334
And it was -- it was awesome.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.834
-And I will say the whole --

00:05:59.834 --> 00:06:01.767
you're on the whole soundtrack,
is you and Maluma.

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:04.100
I mean, this thing is --
it's awesome.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:06.667
-Yeah, it's not like
a Jennifer Lopez J.Lo album

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:09.634
or even a Maluma album.
It's a Kat and Bastian album.

00:06:09.634 --> 00:06:13.334
These are songs that I really
picked for the characters

00:06:13.334 --> 00:06:15.601
and that really kind of like
further along the story,

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.434
just like any good musical.
-Yeah.

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:19.133
-And it really tells
the love story,

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:22.033
the journey of, you know,
kind of finding your true love.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:23.801
-I want to talk about "Marry Me"
when we come back.

00:06:23.801 --> 00:06:25.634
More with Jennifer Lopez
when we come back.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:26.467
Come on!

